They met together in Galilee. Then Jesus said to them, "The Son of Man will be delivered into the hands of men."
They will kill him. On the third day he will rise from the dead." At that, the disciples were filled with grief. Jesus pays the temple tax.
Jesus and his disciples arrived in Capernaum. There, tax collectors came to Peter. They asked him, "Does not your teacher pay the temple tax?"
He answered and said, "Yes, he does." And when Peter was entered into the house, Jesus spoke first. "What do you think, Simon? Of whom do kings of their provinces from tribute or tax? From their own sons or from strangers?"
Peter answered: "From others." And Jesus said to him: "Then, children do not need to pay."
But we don't want to anger them. Go to the lake and cast your line. Take the first fish you catch. Open its mouth. You will find there the exact coin you need. Take it and offer it to them as tax for you and me.
